":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2978,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-05-22T16:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T16:23:23Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-01-26T18:09:14Z"},"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-02-13T00:56:39Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T22:21:10Z","closed_at":"2025-11-11T22:19:25Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.3-stable [77dcf97d8], 4.4-beta3\n- Not reproducible in: 4.2.2-stable [15073afe3]\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you have a node that exports a property of a custom type, and you set that property to point to *any* descendant node, using `Node.duplicate` won't duplicate that property at all, and it will remain `null`.\n\nIf you move the descendant node to anywhere else outside the subtree of the tested node, the issue doesn't happen.\n\nIf you use the editor to duplicate, the issue doesn't happen.\n\nI guess this is related to work that was made regarding node duplication in recent versions (4.3, 4.4), but the issues they fix don't describe this error, so I figured writing a new issue would be better.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIn the MRP, there's a simple scene setup with 4 nodes (Test > CustomNode > Node > Node2).\n\nCustomNode's `prop` points to Node2. The `Test` node tries to duplicate CustomNode, but `prop` remains null. The error \"failed to duplicate\" is output to the console.\n\nReparenting Node2 to Test in the editor makes the error go away.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[duplicate-issue-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18804518/duplicate-issue-mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_ur